      "text": "# Bounded Asynchronous Log Ingestion Service\n\n## Design Overview\n\nThis design builds a production-grade log ingestion service on top of `asyncio.Queue` (the provided implementation). The service must handle:\n\n1. **Backpressure**: When the queue is full, producers must block or shed load gracefully.\n2. **Cancellation**: Tasks waiting on `get()`/`put()` must be cancellable without corrupting state.\n3. **Shutdown**: Graceful drain vs. immediate abort, with proper unblocking of all waiters.\n4. **Retries**: Transient failures in downstream processing must not lose logs.\n5. **Ordering**: FIFO ordering must be preserved for the base queue; priority/LIFO variants have their own semantics.\n\n### Key Architectural Decisions\n\n| Concern | Strategy |\n|---|---|\n| **Backpressure** | Bounded `maxsize`; producers await `put()` which blocks when full. Optional timeout + shed policy. |\n| **Cancellation** | `asyncio.CancelledError` propagates through `put()`/`get()`. The queue's internal `_putters`/`_getters` deques are cleaned up in `except` blocks. We wrap consumer tasks",
